<title>UK: Algeria cuts LPG prices to $167/$175 a tonne.</title>
<headline>Algeria cuts LPG prices to $167/$175 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil and gas company Sonatrach has cut its official posted prices for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) for July.</p>
<p>Propane will be cut by $8 a tonne to $167 a tonne fob Bethioua. And butane will be cut by $5 a tonne to $175 a tonne fob Bethioua.</p>
<p>The premium for loading at Arzew or Skikda will be $5 a tonne.</p>
<p>The prices are effective from July 1.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
